DESCRIPTION:Cabrillo National Monument\nhttps://www.nps.gov/cabr/planyourv
 isit/calendar.htm\n\n\n\nCabrillo National Monument is a hotspot for both
  resident and migrating birds as part of the Pacific Flyway\, a central m
 igration corridor used by billions of birds each year. Its unique ecology
  and position along the coast make Cabrillo an ideal place to observe ter
 restrial and coastal bird species. Join park staff for a one-mile bird wa
 tching hike along the coastal trail. All ages and experience levels are w
 elcome. This is a great opportunity to learn the basics of birding while 
 seeing some of 
URL:https://www.nps.gov/cabr/planyourvisit/calendar.htm
END:VEVENT
